[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Coupled BJT Early charge

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BJT-EARLY-CHARGE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Forward diffusion charge and cross derivative
STATEMENT: >>>
The bounded forward Early BJT profile shall evaluate forward diffusion charge
and its junction and collector-control derivatives consistently with transport,
preserving intrinsic-node polarity and rejecting invalid model domains.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
VAF-only low-injection profile; no claim of full Gummel–Poon qualification.
Implementation: spice_diode.rs, compile.rs, newton.rs, BjtPreparation.cs.
Verification: tests/bjt_coupled_charge.rs and independent ngspice comparisons.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BJT-EARLY-HISTORY-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Shared coupled charge history
STATEMENT: >>>
AC, backward Euler, trapezoidal integration and current observables shall use
the same coupled terminal charge law and accepted history, including midpoint
states, without mutating history on failed Newton or rejected timestep trials.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: newton.rs, api.rs and independent audit modules.
Finite tests do not establish universal convergence or global error bounds.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BJT-AC-ZERO-CONSTRAINT-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Homogeneous row evaluation under unchanged residual policy
STATEMENT: >>>
The sparse complex provider shall evaluate a homogeneous row for its dominant
unknown only when every other numerical coefficient is at most one binary64
epsilon of that coefficient. It shall retain every remaining coefficient and
product, preserve exact singleton consequences, and retain independent
verification of every matrix row under the unchanged componentwise threshold.
Factor-reuse refinement work shall remain bounded to three corrections.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: backend_faer.rs provider-side row evaluation before initial scoring
and after each correction. Verification: complex_refinement_contracts and the
public generated BJT AC request with a grounded zero-phasor supply.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BJT-EARLY-AC-PHASE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Coupled storage current preserves complex phase
STATEMENT: >>>
The public AC terminal-current observable shall retain both complex components
of the Early-effect charge derivative. With an AC-grounded base and collector
phasor a+j*b, its control contribution shall be -omega*k*b+j*omega*k*a,
where k=TF*IS*expm1(VBE/VT)/VA at positive forward bias. The supplying base
source shall balance both components and the ideal control shall draw no current.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: tests/bjt_coupled_charge.rs,
quadrature_control_current_obeys_jomega_charge_and_terminal_kcl.
Finite analytical cases cover LU and Faer at two frequencies and three phases;
they do not establish full Gummel-Poon or arbitrary BJT model qualification.
<<<
